
The Executions Overview in n8n displays a list of all workflow executions, including both successful and failed runs.

By default, the list includes all historical executions stored in the database.

You can scroll or paginate through executions to review older runs.

The details panel allows you to inspect input, output, and errors for each execution.

⚠️ Note: The actual number of executions visible depends on your execution data retention settings
. If pruning or limited storage is configured, older executions may not be available.

Why This Update?

Current documentation does not clearly state that the Executions Overview shows all historical executions.

This creates confusion for new users who expect only recent runs to appear.

Adding this clarification will help users understand the scope of history and how it connects to retention settings.
